<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sheikh Hasina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1947">1947</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sheikh Hasina is a Bangladeshi politician, daughter of the founding leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman</a> and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awami-league">Awami League</a>. She was prime minister from 1996 to 2001 and again from 2009 to 2024, the country's longest-serving head of government, a period of fast economic growth and increasingly authoritarian rule. Mass student-led protests forced her to resign and flee to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in August 2024.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sheikh-hasina.jpg" alt="Sheikh Hasina" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Press Information Department · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sheikh_Hasina_meets_Editors%27_Guild_Bangladesh_and_Journalists%27_Union_Ganabhaban_2024-01-03_(PID-0011626)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
